! mcp_bootstrap_p217.strap -- MCP printed page 217: the tail of the V
! card-scan (V SCAN .. V SC7B, V SC3, V SC0), the job/command card test
! (RJOB, RCOMD, RSWITC, RBREAK) and V SC5 .. V SCR1.
!
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.224, read at 400 dpi, 900/1800 dpi
! for doubtful glyphs.  Header, READ: "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID
! 11D11MCP  CARD ID CA000179  DIST. OF 3/01  3/01  PAGE NUMBER 217"; the
! heading row's LOCATION field is 224237, line 1's word.
!
! THE PAGE.  50 lines, contiguous from 224237.40 to 224273.40 (a half
! word), then blank paper; p.218 line 1 (V SCR3) is at 224274.00.
!   lines  4-5   RJOB / RCOMD DD(BU,48) constants, 48 bits each.
!   lines  6, 47 continuation cards, NAME "-", no location, remark only:
!                compile nothing; kept as comments.
!
! THE "-0212".."-0250" COLUMN is the remark field (one per card,
! numbered); it prints at one of two columns.  Written as the remark.
!
! >>> CARD SERIALS. <<<  Printed "0A000179".."0A000223" (the header
! says CA000179: the round first glyph is the drum's C).  One per line
! except pairs sharing a serial: lines 10/11 (188; line 11 prints
! "0A000186" with worn 8s -- read 188 by the pair pattern, not by ink),
! 18/19 (195), 31/32 (207), 35/36 (210), 42/43 (216).  Asterisks after
! the LOCATION on lines 5, 24 and 44; recorded, not explained.
!
! >>> RJOB AND RCOMD, NOT "RJCB" AND "RCCMD". <<<  The NAME column of
! lines 4/5 prints an open round in both.  Lines 25 and 27 reference
! the same labels and print a closed O ("RJOB", "RCOMD") at 900 dpi;
! the names are JOB / COMD.  The binaries 224241.00 / 224241.60 are
! the lines 4/5 locations either way.
!
! >>> V SQ1 (line 10) and V SC10 (line 19). <<<  Line 10 prints a Q
! with its tail ("SG1" to OCR), the twin of line 46's V SQ2.  Line 19
! prints "V SC1C" with the last glyph identical to the C at 1800 dpi;
! its defining card, p.218 line 23 at 224307.00, prints "V SC10" with
! a closed 0.  Written VSC10.  External; the name does not reach the
! binary.
!
! >>> LINE 34 "V NCP" IS V NOP (224157.40, the p.216 label). <<<
! Octal-field C glyphs (e.g. "COCCC5.CC", "11CCCO.00", "(8)24CC2..")
! are 0 by the octal rule.
!
! >>> TWO HEX BYTES PRINT AN OPEN ROUND THAT IS 0. <<<  Line 11
! (B,$.32) prints "224245.5C C0" and line 34 (LVNI) prints "224157.63
! C9".  At 1800 dpi both are the same open round this page prints in
! octal fields where only 0 can stand (line 3 ".C3", line 11 ".5C"),
! and identical to the true C of line 3's CB- "C9" and line 15's BZAE
! "C0": shape cannot decide.  Settled by assembly: B assembles 00
! (lines 20/39/40 print 00), LVNI assembles 09 (as p.216 / p.218
! print it, e.g. 224207.00 "224210.23 09").  Checked as 00 and 09.
!
! VH is p.213's integer 32; "$.VH" (line 40) is $ plus 32 bits (C22-6531
! printed p.10): 224266.40+.32+.10 = 224267.10.  VNXT is the half word 224456.40 (volume OCR "224456.4C ... V NXT").

VCRD    SYN, (8)5.0                  ! landed; p.100 card "- VCRD SYN,5."
VRDCW   SYN, (8)225236.0             ! "," on line 2, this page's binary
VP      SYN, (8)21.0                 ! $1 -- this page's binary (CB+ J field, SIC,(VP))
VM1     SYN(BU,64), (8)777777.0             ! CB- on line 3, this page's binary
VU      SYN, (8)23.0                 ! $3 -- this page's binary (LVI J field)
VSC     SYN, (8)225250.0             ! LVI on line 7, this page's binary
VS1     SYN, (8)32.0                 ! $10 -- this page's binary (LX J field)
VS2     SYN, (8)33.0                 ! $11 -- LV on line 29 prints 000033.22, BIT-EXACT
VT5     SYN, (8)31.0                 ! $9 -- this page's binary (LV/LVNI J field)
VTX     SYN, (8)225246.0             ! LX on line 12, this page's binary
VTX1    SYN, (8)225247.0             ! LX on line 8, this page's binary
VSQ1    SYN, (8)224322.0             ! SIC on line 10, BIT-EXACT
VSC10   SYN, (8)224307.0             ! CB+ on line 19; p.218 line 23 "V SC10" 224307.00
VNXT    SYN, (8)224456.40            ! CB+ on line 32 (224456.43 = .40 + VP's J), half word
VNOP    SYN, (8)224157.40            ! LVNI on line 34; p.216 "V NOP" at 224157.40
VNX     SYN, (8)5.0                  ! CB+ on line 36: VNX+VSC = 225255.0
VH      SYN, 32                      ! p.213 line 7 "V H SYN,32", an INTEGER; ".V H" is 32 bits
SPRIMR  SYN, (8)215571.0             ! landed
SPRIME  SYN, (8)215570.0             ! landed
SJC1    SYN, 76.32                   ! landed; printed p.106 line 8
VSCR3   SYN, (8)224274.0             ! BBZ on line 46; p.218 line 1 "V SCR3" 224274.00
VSQ2    SYN, (8)224311.40            ! BBZ on line 46; p.218 "V SQ2" 224311.40

        SLC, (8)224237.40
